WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Thread keeps your coding agent aligned with decisions written in Obsidian. This captured walkthrough shows the real plugin, connected to MongoDB Atlas, with your goal beside the work.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
When the decision changes, Thread excludes the dependent outdated procedure. Here, the string false means active. The historical procedure was seeded, and its invalidation is recorded.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
A real Codex experiment raised acceptance from eleven to sixteen out of sixteen. An independent review approved the change. Atlas retains the checks, experiment, and learned review procedure.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Brief retrieves current decisions and supported procedures into a readable note, with source links and selection reasons. Copy it into your coding workflow. No coding agent runs until you start one.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Eighteen fresh sessions tested isolated code. No memory passed zero of six. Both notes conditions passed six. Requirement access helps here; added procedural benefit remains unproven.
